Description:
    Generates view files for each question page defined in an ApplicationFormFlow.
    Each view includes the appropriate form fields based on the ApplicationForm model's
    attribute types, and an en.yml locale file with default translations.

Usage:
    bin/rails generate strata:application_form_views FLOW_NAME FORM_NAME

Examples:
    bin/rails generate strata:application_form_views LeaveApplicationFlow LeaveApplicationForm
    bin/rails generate strata:application_form_views SampleFlow SampleApplicationForm
    bin/rails generate strata:application_form_views PassportFlow PassportApplicationForm

Field Type Detection:
    The generator inspects the ApplicationForm model to determine the appropriate
    form helper for each field:

    Strata attributes:
        memorable_date       - f.memorable_date
        money                - f.money_field
        tax_id               - f.tax_id_field
        us_date              - f.date_picker
        name                 - f.name
        address              - f.address_fields

    Standard types:
        enum                 - f.fieldset with f.radio_button for each value
        boolean              - f.yes_no
        date / datetime      - f.date_picker
        text                 - f.text_area
        integer / decimal    - f.text_field with inputmode: "numeric"
        string (default)     - f.text_field

    Skipped/Unsupported fields:
        Fields ending in _attributes (nested attributes)
        Fields backed by has_one_attached or has_many_attached
        Fields that exist on the flow but not on the ApplicationForm model

This will create:
    An edit_<page_name>.html.erb view file for each question page, placed in
    app/views/<form_name_pluralized>/. Each view uses strata_form_with, includes
    an i18n heading, the detected form fields, and a form_buttons partial.

    A config/locales/<form_name_pluralized>/en.yml file with default translations
    for page titles and enum labels. If the locale file already exists, new
    translations are merged without overwriting existing entries.
